{#
  One photograph, with its credit underneath.

  The credit is not decoration and not optional: these are other people's
  photographs, published under the Unsplash licence, which asks that the
  photographer be named. It is stored on the attachment as post meta at import and
  read back here, so a photograph can never appear on the site without it.

  The plate crops to a ratio — 3:4 standing, 3:2 lying down — and that is where
  `#[AsImageSize]` runs out. Two ratios cannot come from one registered size, and
  a size registered now would apply to nothing already uploaded. So the crop is
  asked for here through `image_url()` and the transformer produces it. With no
  transformer configured the source URL comes back and the page still renders.

  It is also the difference between cropping and appearing to crop: `object-fit`
  gives the right shape by downloading the whole photograph and discarding
  whatever falls outside the ratio.
#}
{# `image` is a Demo\Models\Photograph, the #[AsTimberModel] class of attachments. #}
{% set orientation = image.orientation %}
{% set credit = image.credit %}

{# The crop: 3:4 standing, 3:2 lying down, at two widths rather than 1x/2x. 1200
   is the widest crop every original here can fill without being upscaled, which a
   density descriptor would hide. Photograph::plate() builds it, so the job that
   warms the plates of a project asks for the same URLs. #}
{% set plate = image.plate(600) %}
{% set src = image_url(image, plate) %}
{% set src_wide = image_url(image, image.plate(1200)) %}

<figure>
  <div class="plate plate--{{ orientation }}">
    {% if image %}
      <img
        src="{{ src }}"
        srcset="{{ src }} 600w, {{ src_wide }} 1200w"
        sizes="{{ sizes|default('(min-width: 48rem) 60vw, 100vw') }}"
        width="600"
        height="{{ plate.h }}"
        alt="{{ image.alt ? : caption|default('') }}"
        loading="{{ loading|default('lazy') }}"
        decoding="async" />
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <figcaption class="credit">
    {% if caption is defined and caption %}
      <span>{{ caption }}</span>
    {% endif %}

    {% if credit %}
      <span>
        Photo&nbsp;:{% if credit.url %}
          <a href="{{ credit.url }}" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">
            {{ credit.title }}
          </a>
        {% else %}
          {{ credit.title }}
        {% endif %}/ Unsplash
      </span>
    {% endif %}
  </figcaption>
</figure>
